<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin's staff checks 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin's staff checks 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian President Boris Yeltsin's staff is now checking the 1997 budget, Itar-Tass news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It quoted presidential spokesman Sergei Yastrzhembsky as saying he expected Yeltsin to sign the budget into law next week.</p>
<p>&quot;The President supports the budget produced by the government,&quot; Yastrzhembsky was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>The budget, approved by the Federation Council, the upper house of parliament last week, envisages a deficit of 3.5 percent of gross domestic product, by Russian calculations.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
